WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.960
Cut the cable.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Pull the plug.

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.520
Bring it back.

4
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.340
Once makes sure every driver
is charged exactly once.

5
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:13.813
The EU now has more than a
million public charge points,

6
00:00:13.853 --> 00:00:15.413
and every new one must take

7
00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:17.760
payment from anyone
who drives up.

8
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.773
But chargers drop offline.

9
00:00:19.813 --> 00:00:22.613
When they reconnect, they
replay what they missed,

10
00:00:22.653 --> 00:00:24.053
and payment code that trusts

11
00:00:24.093 --> 00:00:26.213
those messages charges twice,

12
00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:28.953
or charges the wrong person.

13
00:00:28.967 --> 00:00:29.967
Watch.

14
00:00:30.007 --> 00:00:31.487
A real test payment puts a

15
00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:33.967
fifty-euro hold
on charger seven.

16
00:00:34.007 --> 00:00:35.407
We cut the cable.

17
00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:38.154
The first driver unplugs
while it's offline,

18
00:00:38.194 --> 00:00:40.074
and the next driver pays.

19
00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:41.567
When the link comes back,

20
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:45.167
the naive code bills driver
B for driver A's energy,

21
00:00:45.207 --> 00:00:46.527
and Stripe says:

22
00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.547
succeeded.

23
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.020
So we hand the
problem to an agent.

24
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.060
Once writes its
own settlement code

25
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.060
and runs it inside
a CreateOS sandbox,

26
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.380
with no internet and no keys,

27
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.340
next to twelve simulated
chargers it can cut,

28
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.740
reboot and reconnect at will.

29
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.340
Thirty fault storms.

30
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.660
The naive code survives four.

31
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.993
The agent rewrites it,

32
00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.980
and the storms run again
inside the sandbox:

33
00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.660
thirty out of thirty.

34
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.420
Zero double charges.

35
00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.260
Zero stranded holds.

36
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.920
Only then does it ship.

37
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:22.113
The agent never touches money.

38
00:01:22.153 --> 00:01:25.073
Its code can only
emit capture intents;

39
00:01:25.113 --> 00:01:27.553
the host executes
each one once,

40
00:01:27.593 --> 00:01:30.193
and Stripe witnesses
every capture.

41
00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.793
Probe the boundary yourself:

42
00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:35.153
the code can't reach the
network, can't read a file,

43
00:01:35.193 --> 00:01:37.420
and is stopped
after one second.

44
00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.553
The whole stack, CreateOS,
OpenRouter and Vercel,

45
00:01:41.593 --> 00:01:43.473
came from Stripe Projects,

46
00:01:43.513 --> 00:01:46.293
starting in an
empty directory.

47
00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.567
Same charger.

48
00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.007
Same storm.

49
00:01:49.047 --> 00:01:53.087
Every driver charged for their
own energy, exactly once.

50
00:01:53.127 --> 00:01:54.127
Once:

51
00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:57.007
payment code that proves
itself before it ships.

52
00:01:57.047 --> 00:02:01.587
Try it now at once-seven
dot vercel dot app.
